[section, $md:
    # HTML components

    A reusable component is a value made from templates, types and functions.
    Its HTML, stylesheet dependencies and other outputs remain explicit.
    A const function can construct the value, and the entry can compose
    several components into a page.

    This guide describes the intended `@html` component layer, including
    APIs not yet implemented. See the @../../progress (progress matrix)
    for the currently available language and package surface.
]

